    "intro_html":  "Pelau is Trinidad\u0027s Sunday pot, and it starts with an act that looks like a mistake: sugar melted in hot oil until it turns almost black. Chicken hits that caramel and takes the color, then rice, pigeon peas, coconut milk and sweet potato all cook down in the same pot until it is one thick, brown, sweet-and-savory thing. Each bowl lands \u003cstrong\u003e700 calories and 30 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$3.75\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). Big flavor, one pot, fourteen dinners.",
